language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ crew: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Assign flight attendants to flights. Each flight needs a certain number of cabin crew, and they have to speak certain languages. A flight has exactly the required number of cabin crew, and at least the required number of each of the other kinds of attendant (stewards, hostesses, French, Spanish and German speakers); one person can count towards several of them. Every cabin crew member has at least two flights off after an attended flight, so nobody attends more than one of any three consecutive flights.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `crew.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/crew.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `crew_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py crew.json
$   savilerow model.eprime crew_1.param -run-solver

$ attributes_dim1: the number of people (derived from the data); attributes_dim2: the number of attributes (derived)
given attributes_dim1, attributes_dim2 : int(1..)
$ attributes[p,k]: 1 if person p has attribute k, indices 1-based: 1 steward, 2 hostess, 3 speaks French, 4 speaks Spanish, 5 speaks German
given attributes : matrix indexed by [int(1..attributes_dim1), int(1..attributes_dim2)] of int(0..1)
$ required_crew_dim1: the number of flights (derived from the data); required_crew_dim2: the number of requirements (derived)
given required_crew_dim1, required_crew_dim2 : int(1..)
$ required_crew[f,k]: for flight f (1-based), k=1 the number of cabin crew, k=2 to 6 the minimum numbers of stewards, hostesses, French, Spanish and German speakers
given required_crew : matrix indexed by [int(1..required_crew_dim1), int(1..required_crew_dim2)] of int(0..)

$ crew[f,p]: person p is assigned to flight f
find crew : matrix indexed by [int(1..required_crew_dim1), int(1..attributes_dim1)] of bool

such that
$ each flight has exactly the required number of cabin crew
forAll f : int(1..required_crew_dim1) . (sum p : int(1..attributes_dim1) . toInt(crew[f,p])) = required_crew[f,1],
$ each flight has at least the required number of stewards
forAll f : int(1..required_crew_dim1) . (sum p : int(1..attributes_dim1) . toInt(crew[f,p]) * attributes[p,1]) >= required_crew[f,2],
$ each flight has at least the required number of hostesses
forAll f : int(1..required_crew_dim1) . (sum p : int(1..attributes_dim1) . toInt(crew[f,p]) * attributes[p,2]) >= required_crew[f,3],
$ each flight has at least the required number of French speakers
forAll f : int(1..required_crew_dim1) . (sum p : int(1..attributes_dim1) . toInt(crew[f,p]) * attributes[p,3]) >= required_crew[f,4],
$ each flight has at least the required number of Spanish speakers
forAll f : int(1..required_crew_dim1) . (sum p : int(1..attributes_dim1) . toInt(crew[f,p]) * attributes[p,4]) >= required_crew[f,5],
$ each flight has at least the required number of German speakers
forAll f : int(1..required_crew_dim1) . (sum p : int(1..attributes_dim1) . toInt(crew[f,p]) * attributes[p,5]) >= required_crew[f,6],
$ nobody attends more than one of any three consecutive flights: for every window of three consecutive flights, each person is assigned to at most one of them
forAll p : int(1..attributes_dim1) . forAll f : int(1..required_crew_dim1) . (sum g : int(1..required_crew_dim1) . toInt(g >= f /\ g <= f + 2) * toInt(crew[g,p])) <= 1
